<span id="mouse-gestures-title" class="anchor-alias" aria-hidden="true"
></span><span id="gesture-close-title" class="anchor-alias" aria-hidden="true"
></span>
<section
  class="feature-copy-grid feature-copy-grid--top"
  aria-labelledby="gesture-start-title"
>
  <div>
    <p class="section-kicker">start anywhere</p><h2 id="gesture-start-title">
      The page becomes the control.
    </h2>
  </div>
  <div class="feature-copy-list">
    <article>
      <h3>With a physical mouse</h3><p>
        Hold the right mouse button, draw the gesture over the active page, then
        release. A normal right-click without a drag still opens the page’s
        usual menu.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>With a trackpad</h3><p>
        Hold Alt on Windows or Option on macOS, click and hold with one finger,
        then drag and release. A click without the drag stays an ordinary click.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Only the finished motion runs</h3><p>
        Blanc waits for release before acting. Unassigned gestures and drawings
        with more than three directions do nothing.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="feature-copy-grid" aria-labelledby="gesture-custom-title">
  <div>
    <p class="section-kicker">make it yours</p><h2 id="gesture-custom-title">
      Draw the shortcut you want to remember.
    </h2>
  </div>
  <div class="feature-copy-list">
    <article>
      <h3>Begin with four defaults</h3><p>
        Left goes Back, right goes Forward, up opens a New tab, and down closes
        the current tab. Restore defaults brings these four motions back at any
        time.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Add turns when one direction is not enough</h3><p>
        In Settings → General, choose Add gesture and draw up to three
        directions. Pick its action, save it, and it is ready on the active
        page.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Choose from nine browser actions</h3><p>
        Assign Back, Forward, Reload, New tab, Close tab, Reopen closed tab,
        Previous tab, Next tab, or Open Island. Existing gestures can be
        reassigned or removed.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<aside class="truth-note" aria-labelledby="gesture-note-title">
  <p class="section-kicker">good to know</p><h2 id="gesture-note-title">
    Off until you ask for it. Local when you do.
  </h2>
  <p>
    Mouse gestures are disabled by default. Turn them on in Settings → General.
    Your enabled state and assignments stay on this device rather than following
    you through Sync.
  </p>
  <a
    class="text-link"
    href="/support#island"
    data-track="feature_cta_click"
    data-feature="mouse-gestures"
    data-cta-position="related-feature"
    >See the Island these gestures can open <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span
    ></a
  >
</aside>
